# CLI model and reference-video export

Status: DONE
Milestone: Reusable offline model-review pipeline
Dependencies: 13_BLENDER_MODEL_RUNTIME.todo, 20_CORE_MOTION_UPGRADE.todo

## Purpose
Let another model-authoring session render a supplied GLB against a reference recording without
opening Studio, producing synthetic video and inspectable evidence rather than claiming perfection.

## Tasks
- [x] Inspect existing headless PNG/report support and offline verification patterns.
- [x] Add frame-by-frame, source-clock export with isolated native tracking.
- [x] Encode and verify an MP4; produce a source-private aggregate report and optional PNG.
- [x] Protect original inputs/existing outputs and clean up interrupted/failed exports.
- [x] Add CLI/encoder/lifecycle regressions and exercise the supplied model/recording.
- [x] Document copyable cross-directory commands and model-review limitations.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Every frame in the selected source interval is inferred/rendered once, without real-time drops.
- [x] Source-relative timing is explicit and output duration/frame count are verified.
- [x] Only synthetic images enter output; no input audio/raw pixels/landmark dump is included.
- [x] Model/profile/reference inputs and pre-existing output files cannot be overwritten.
- [x] Native failures, invalid input, cancellation and incomplete output are explicit.
- [x] Another chat can invoke the isolated Python executable with absolute paths from its own base.
- [x] Reports distinguish tracking availability, structural validation and subjective visual approval.

